Result: exit 0. The real K1 three-Broker E2E started the TCP OffsetCommit response-loss proxy. The first Java smoke process reached ACK_UNKNOWN after applying the source entry: Broker group offset 2, Target Store source offset 1, test Owner epoch 1. The proxy had received but withheld the Broker OffsetCommit response. The harness SIGKILLed that Java process and confirmed its Gradle task did not return success. A fresh Java process then opened the same RocksDB path, checked the persisted Broker cluster/topic/partition identity and source state, acquired a higher test Owner epoch, replayed the exact source command, reused its stored result without another Store mutation, and confirmed group offset 2. The proxy recorded seven withheld OffsetCommit Broker responses during the run.

