This verifies single-Shard source-ACK uncertainty across an actual JVM SIGKILL and fresh-process RocksDB reopen against a real Broker. The source/Owner authority used by the smoke is still test-provided; the fresh process seeds an in-memory Owner lease fixture from the persisted epoch. This does not verify a live Oxia lease takeover, Claim/Admission/Producer ownership crash, uncertain Store write, multi-Shard sibling isolation combined with Broker response loss, shared-channel teardown, the full D2 matrix, or centralized validation. D2 remains IN_PROGRESS / PENDING_CENTRAL_VALIDATION.

